From: Chris Painter <chris@gobehindtheproduct.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gradio_app: drop enable_face_tracking + head_tracker_type kwargs

Upstream bug at commit 3785255: gradio_app.py passes
`enable_face_tracking=` and `head_tracker_type=` to ClawBodyCore(...),
but ClawBodyCore.__init__ does not accept either parameter, so launching
the Gradio UI with `clawbody --gradio` raises TypeError immediately:

  ClawBodyCore.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument
  'enable_face_tracking'

Workaround: drop both kwargs from the launch site. Face tracking is
unaffected for sim-only users (the simulator has no camera); when
upstream wires the kwargs through to ClawBodyCore, this patch will
fail to apply and we'll know to drop it.

Apply with: patch -p1 < 0001-drop-unsupported-face-tracking-kwargs.patch
---
 src/reachy_mini_openclaw/gradio_app.py | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/reachy_mini_openclaw/gradio_app.py b/src/reachy_mini_openclaw/gradio_app.py
--- a/src/reachy_mini_openclaw/gradio_app.py
+++ b/src/reachy_mini_openclaw/gradio_app.py
@@ -59,8 +59,6 @@ def launch_gradio(
                 robot_name=robot_name,
                 enable_camera=enable_camera,
                 enable_openclaw=enable_openclaw,
-                enable_face_tracking=enable_face_tracking,
-                head_tracker_type=head_tracker_type,
             )

             # Run in background thread
